{
    "name": "E2E Zoho Books - new contact",
    "description": "Provokes the NewContact polling trigger: waits for the baseline tick, creates a customer, asserts the contact the trigger emits and deletes it.",
    "notes": {
        "55b513cd-ca0b-4fac-b5a5-5096c6e1a8d1": {
            "x": 64,
            "y": 512,
            "width": 672,
            "height": 256,
            "content": "## ⚠️ Test data assumption + timing\n\n**Organization ID** `20111141498` is set on the New Contact trigger and on the Create/Delete components. It must be an organization of the connected Zoho Books account — on another tenant replace it in all three places.\n\n**Do not remove the Wait.** New Contact records the existing contacts on its first tick and only emits contacts created later; a contact created at flow start lands in that baseline and never fires.\n\nThe trigger watches customers only. Another flow creating customers in the same organization at the same time can fire it first and fail the name assertion — run this flow on its own. The cleanup reads the **trigger's** `contact_id`, so it doubles as the proof that the trigger fired."
        }
    },
